## 5. Build and registration
- `Makefile`: `build` only builds `./cmd/partio`. `test` is `go test ./... -v` and `lint` is `golangci-lint run`, so a new package and cmd are tested and linted automatically.
- `.goreleaser.yml`: one build, `./cmd/partio`. The minion cmds are **not** released and should not be added.
- No list needs a new entry. The minion cmds run in CI through `go run ./cmd/minion-...` in `.github/workflows/*.yml` (for example `deadcode-audit.yml:211`, `e2e-audit.yml:147`, `checks.yml:~128`). Add a workflow step only if you want minion-review to run in CI.

## 6. Clock injection
There is no precedent in the repo: nothing uses a `now func() time.Time`, a clock interface, `time.DateOnly`, or `Format("2006-01-02")`. Every production use calls `time.Now()` directly (`internal/session/*.go`, `internal/hooks/commit_cache.go`, `internal/hooks/postcommit.go`, `internal/checkpoint/prune.go`). You will be setting the pattern. A `Now func() time.Time` field on Config (nil meaning `time.Now`), with `.UTC().Format(time.DateOnly)`, would fit the existing `HTTPClient` "nil means default" convention.

